// The 3M-iteration integer loop from docs/reviews/language-design-review.md's F2 diagnosis
// ("roughly 4-5x slower than CPython... 28x slower" per the two independent reviews) and
// docs/DESIGN.md's interpreter-speed entry -- a `for` loop doing nothing but the loop
// machinery itself and one addition, so its time is almost entirely interpreter overhead,
// not program work. Compare against `fib(27)` (recursive, no loop) to see the two costs
// separately: `time ./ziman tests/bench/loop_bench.zm`.
fn main() {
    var sum = 0
    for i in 0..3000000 {
        sum = sum + i
    }
    print(sum)
}
